------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ITEM 4 (recalibrated).  The exact finite-height variance is now
      V(T) = (1/(2 pi^2)) [ log L + M + C_pp + 1 + eps(T) ],   L = log(T/2 pi),  M+C_pp = 0.4009679
  so the classical asymptotic (1/(2 pi^2)) log log T carries a relative deficit
      (1 + M + C_pp + log(1 - log(2pi)/log T)) / log log T   ->   1.4009679 / log log T.
